<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What Is a Box Room?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A box room is the smallest bedroom in a British house, often above the stairs or over the front door. Many are around 2 to 2.5 metres on each side, and some have a bulkhead, a raised box in the floor over the top of the staircase. Most fit a single bed and little else, so layout matters.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Box Room Layout Guide</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Start with a plan before you buy anything. The diagram below shows a typical box room with a single bed, a walkway and a wardrobe on the bulkhead.</p>



