<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For comparison, the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/technical-housing-standards-nationally-described-space-standard/technical-housing-standards-nationally-described-space-standard" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nationally Described Space Standard</a> for new homes in England asks for a single bedroom to have a floor area of at least 7.5 m² and to be at least 2.15 m wide. The standard applies to new dwellings, not existing homes, and many older box rooms are smaller, which is why the ideas below focus on beds and storage that use height instead of floor.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Which Bed Fits a Box Room?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The bed decides the whole layout. These are common UK mattress sizes and how each one works in a small room.</p>



